<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        NEW FILE, 2026-08-28. Mirrors a principal's approval of an Underwriting__c record back
        onto its parent Opportunity, replacing the three-hop chain that used to run through
        Opportunity.Underwriting_Approval -> Opportunity_UW_Approved_Notify ->
        ApprovalAuditService(gate='Underwriting'). That old chain is now dead:
        Opportunity.Underwriting_Approval is deactivated (see that file's header) and no
        Opportunity ProcessInstance for this gate will ever exist again.

        🔴 SEPARATE FLOW - flows/Underwriting_Opp_Sync IS NOT EXTENDED. Four independent
        reasons, all still true at time of writing:
          1. ENTRY SEMANTICS. Underwriting_Opp_Sync has no entry filter and no
             doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria - it fires on every save. This mirror stamp
             MUST be transition-scoped: Opportunity_UW_Approved_Notify (the market-data freeze)
             is itself entry-scoped on Opportunity.Underwriting_Status__c transitioning TO
             'Approved by Principals', and only fires once per genuine transition.
          2. Underwriting_Opp_Sync's own <description> states "Underwriting_Status__c is
             deliberately NOT synced - the approval process owns it." Under this design the
             approval (via this flow) still owns it - extending that flow would force retracting
             a decision that is still true.
          3. A flow has ONE <start>; the approved path needs a different entry filter than an
             ordinary save, so it needs its own trigger.
          4. BLAST RADIUS. Underwriting_Opp_Sync pushes the deal's headline numbers and is live
             and working. This flow can be deactivated for diagnosis without taking that down.

        🔴 THIS CONTRACT IS PINNED - the developer stream is building UnderwritingApprovalStampService
        to it; do not vary the action name or input variable name:
            Apex action:     UnderwritingApprovalStampService
                              (label 'Stamp Underwriting Approval To Deal')
            input variable:  underwritingId (Id)

        ENTRY: Stage__c CHANGED TO 'Approved' - doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria = true,
        so this fires on the transition only, never on the initial submission save (which would
        wrongly re-stamp/clear the parent) and never on an unrelated edit while already Approved.

        🔴 NO REJECTED BRANCH. Per user decision D2, Stage__c never changes on rejection (it
        stays 'In Progress'), so there is nothing for a Stage__c-keyed flow to see. This is not
        an oversight - see approvalProcesses/Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval's own header
        for the accepted, documented loss (Opportunity.Underwriting_Complete__c is no longer
        auto-cleared on reject).

        🔴 runInMode = SystemModeWithoutSharing IS MANDATORY, MATCHING Underwriting_Opp_Sync AND
        LOI_Approval_Stamp. This flow runs as the APPROVER, and the approving principals are
        deliberately read-only on Opportunity (measured, see MarketDataSnapshotService.cls /
        ApprovalAuditService.cls headers). Without SystemModeWithoutSharing the downstream write
        silently does nothing.

        🔴 THE PARENT WRITE IS DONE IN APEX (UnderwritingApprovalStampService), NOT IN A FLOW
        recordUpdate. This repo has measured that SystemModeWithoutSharing on the FLOW does not,
        by itself, lift the access mode far enough for a read-only approver's write to stick -
        AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE must be stated at the DML itself (see ApprovalAuditService.cls
        header). Routing through the proven Apex path also lets one class own the "ONE DML for
        all four mirror fields" contract that Opportunity_UW_Approved_Notify's own
        entry-scoping depends on - see that flow's <description> and
        UnderwritingApprovalStampService's own header for why a second, later write would arrive
        on a save the freeze flow's entry filter can no longer see.

        ⚠ DO NOT ADD ANY OTHER PARENT WRITE TO THIS FLOW OR CALL A SECOND ACTION AFTER THIS ONE
        THAT ALSO TOUCHES THE OPPORTUNITY. Opportunity_UW_Approved_Notify's
        doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria = true depends on the mirror stamp landing in
        exactly one Opportunity DML; a second write consumes the transition before the freeze
        flow's entry filter can see it.

        DEPLOY ORDER. This flow depends on UnderwritingApprovalStampService (Apex, developer
        stream) already being deployed - the actionCalls below resolve the Apex action by name
        at deploy/activation time.
    -->
    <actionCalls>
        <name>Stamp_Underwriting_Approval</name>
        <label>Stamp Underwriting Approval To Deal</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <actionName>UnderwritingApprovalStampService</actionName>
        <actionType>apex</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>underwritingId</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>UnderwritingApprovalStampService</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Underwriting Approval Sync {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Underwriting Approval Sync</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <runInMode>SystemModeWithoutSharing</runInMode>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Stamp_Underwriting_Approval</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>true</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Stage__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Approved</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>Underwriting__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
